  display.print("BpM");
  display.setTextSize(2);
  display.setCursor(10, 11);
  display.print(SpO2);
  display.print("%");
  display.setCursor(80, 11);
  display.print(avBPM);
  display.display();
}

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  if(!display.begin(SSD1306_SWITCHCAPVCC, 0x3C)) {
    for(;;);
  }
  display.clearDisplay();
  display.display();
}

void loop() {
  // ... existing logic ...
}
```

PARAGRAPH 8
Ensure your SDA is connected to A4 and SCL to A5 on the Pro Mini. These are the default I2C pins for the ATmega328P used on the Pro Mini.

PARAGRAPH 9
Because the Pro Mini has limited RAM, minimize the use of `String` class objects as seen in your original code. Direct print calls (e.g., `display.print(avBPM)`) are much safer for stability.

PARAGRAPH 10
If the screen does not initialize, check the I2C address of your SSD1315. It is usually 0x3C, but some modules may be 0x3D. If 0x3C fails, try changing the address in `display.begin()`.

